<title>USA: Sequa Q1 net profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>Sequa Q1 net profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sequa Corp</p>
<p>		   Report for the Three Months Ended March 31</p>
<p>			(In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>				  1997			   1996</p>
<p> Sales		    $373,328			$349,126</p>
<p> Costs and expenses    358,939			 339,004</p>
<p> Operating income	 14,389			  10,122</p>
<p>Other income/(expense)</p>
<p>   Interest expense   (12,494)			(13,248)</p>
<p>   Interest income	 1,288			   1,040</p>
<p>   Other, net		  842			   (317)</p>
<p>Income/(loss) before</p>
<p>   taxes		     4,025			 (2,403)</p>
<p> Income tax provision  (2,500)			 (1,350)</p>
<p> Net income/(loss)	 1,525			 (3,753)</p>
<p>Net income/(loss)</p>
<p>   per share		   .08			   (.46)</p>
<p>NOTE: Results for both periods include costs from Gas Turbine unit stemming from litigation with Pratt &amp; Whitney unit of United Technologies Corp. That reduced operating income by $3.1 million for the first quarter of 1997 and by $5.2 million for the first quarter of 1996.</p>
</text>
